          "line_end": 6,
          "truncated": false
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "docs/knowledge-base/architecture.md::stack",
        "source": "docs/knowledge-base/architecture.md",
        "kind": "verbatim_excerpt",
        "heading": "Stack",
        "text": "## Stack - **Next.js 16** (App Router) + **React 19**, deployed on **Vercel**. TypeScript throughout. - **Zustand 5** for transient client exploration state (`lib/stores/round.ts`). - **Sucrase** for in-browser TSX transpilation of generated components. - **@vercel/analytics** for usage tracking. - **Claude Sonnet** (Anthropic) as the primary for critique, directions, and code generation, with GPT-4o fallback when configured, behind typed provider interfaces with mock + fixture fallbacks. Note: React is used two ways — the app itself (Next.js/React) and a separately vendored React runtime inlined into the preview iframe (see Live-mount preview below). There is no separate Vite app in this repo; the standalone Vite prototype Bryan saw earlier lived outside this pipeline.",
        "evidence": {
          "file": "docs/knowledge-base/architecture.md",
          "sha256": "1497944060481389639f54b29cc4b5c0e3b3e9bc1b5e8c0da6d0eba07adc84d4",
          "line_start": 7,
          "line_end": 20,
          "truncated": false
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "docs/knowledge-base/roadmap-and-open-work.md::roadmap_open_work",
        "source": "docs/knowledge-base/roadmap-and-open-work.md",
        "kind": "verbatim_excerpt",
        "heading": "Roadmap & Open Work",
        "text": "# Roadmap & Open Work What is built vs. still open, and what's paused. Grounded in `main`, status checked 2026-08-27.",
        "evidence": {
          "file": "docs/knowledge-base/roadmap-and-open-work.md",
          "sha256": "30cd5fa747013fd2be18f6897e58ce08ec5174b28e3f2cfc99db077910059189",
          "line_start": 1,
          "line_end": 4,
          "truncated": false
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "docs/release-plan.md::implementation_status_as_of_2026_08_26",
        "source": "docs/release-plan.md",
        "kind": "verbatim_excerpt",
        "heading": "Implementation status as of 2026-08-26",
        "text": "### Implementation status as of 2026-08-26 Implemented on `main`: screenshot intake and natural-dimension capture; real Claude critique and direction generation; selected-direction streamed code generation; live-mount preview with source fallback; per-exploration viewport inference, correction, and locking; fixed-box `Source` / `Iteration` comparison; and a client-generated ZIP containing runnable source plus the full exploration context. The canonical V0 flow is transient and does not persist screenshots, approvals, or history. Remaining for V1: validate the complete loop against a real project and evaluate whether content-width autocrop plus a confidence flag is needed beyond the current natural-dimension viewport model. Optional ComfyUI clarification remains a graceful enhancement, not a blocker for the core comparison loop.",
        "evidence": {
          "file": "docs/release-plan.md",
          "sha256": "a145c9ddf896fa0629ed8a29f521fce53f65a413e20e2d05f5151bd8a4ec8a71",
          "line_start": 11,
          "line_end": 16,
          "truncated": false
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "docs/release-plan.md::next_decision_point",
        "source": "docs/release-plan.md",
        "kind": "verbatim_excerpt",
        "heading": "Next decision point",
        "text": "### Next decision point Once v1 has run on at least one real project, revisit: whether the 2-3 directions target needs to flex, whether a paid 21st.dev tier is warranted, and how the success bar should evolve for v2.",
        "evidence": {
          "file": "docs/release-plan.md",
          "sha256": "a145c9ddf896fa0629ed8a29f521fce53f65a413e20e2d05f5151bd8a4ec8a71",
          "line_start": 59,
          "line_end": 62,
          "truncated": false
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "docs/release-plan.md::purpose",
        "source": "docs/release-plan.md",
